<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>More Data is Better: Believing all data is useful; students must understand that irrelevant features (noise) can degrade model performance.</li>
        <li>Cleaning as a One-off: Viewing cleaning as the first step only, rather than an iterative process throughout model development.</li>
        <li>Linearity: Assuming all relationships in nature are linear; identifying when Linear Regression is an inappropriate model.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

